{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - Lifecycle - IDP - Okta Identity Provider Created",
	"Description": "A new identity provider was added to the Okta org. An adversary-controlled IdP is a federated back door: once it is trusted, they can mint assertions for any user it is allowed to assert for and never touch a password or a factor.\n\nEvent type: system.idp.lifecycle.create\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/persistence_new_okta_identity_provider_added_by_admin/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/tree/main/rules/integrations/okta/persistence_new_okta_identity_provider_added_by_admin.toml\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
